cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "spot_micro_rl: Reinforcement Learning for SpotMicro Quadruped Locomotion"
message: "If you use this software or its trained checkpoints, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: "V68"
date-released: "2026-04-12"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/etnlwind/spot_micro_rl"
authors:
  - family-names: "RYU"
    given-names: "Sangjin"
    email: "etnlwind@gmail.com"
    alias: "etnlwind"
abstract: >
  spot_micro_rl is a research repository for training a deployable
  quadruped locomotion policy for the SpotMicro open-hardware robot,
  built on NVIDIA Isaac Lab. Over 68 iterated experiments (V1~V68),
  the project progressed from basic standing to a symmetric trot
  capable of 0.308 m/s forward walking. V68 introduces a Reference
  Trajectory Tracking approach that mines and symmetrizes a rollout
  from a previous high-quality policy (V63.I) and lets RL track it,
  resolving the symmetry/quality tradeoff that reward engineering
  alone could not. The best checkpoint is preserved at
  `checkpoints/V68_model_2500_best.pt`.
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - quadruped
  - locomotion
  - SpotMicro
  - Isaac Lab
  - rsl_rl
  - reference-tracking
  - imitation-learning
  - sim-to-real
